A||||8||Simple Fiero||Clutch slipping||||1||
Z||000000||Simple Fiero||10-16-2001||01:30 PM||||On Saturday I noticed that my clutch fluid was low so I bought some Dot3 and added it to the thingie. on sunday I took it for a drive and I was leaving the grocery store and popped into 1st and it jumped to red line and then into 2nd it went right to redline and in 3rd it went to 3grand. but I didn't seem to be going anywhere(I was moving but it seemed very slow). And today i was coming to work got to a hill in 5th and gave it some power and my revs went up but my speedo didn't really go any where, maybe 5 kms that is it, but my speedo jumped to about 3000-3500. And I was only going about 90km. I think my clutch maybe slipping I really hope that isn't it, cause I can't afford 1000 bucks to get it fixed, was wondering what you guys think. is it possible that I got air in the system, this never did this till I added the new fluid.<BR>88 coupe, 5 speed, 4cyl<P>thanks <BR>Craig||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||10-16-2001||02:14 PM||||Someone correct me if I'm wrong, but I believe air in the clutch hydraulics won't make the clutch slip.  The clutch is engaged by the pressure plate and the hydraulics from the clutch pedal release the clutch.  If you have a hydraulic problem, then your clutch won't disengage fully, but it shouldn't affect it's engaged holding power.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||10-16-2001||03:48 PM||||Correct. If it's slipping, the pressure plate isn't gripping like it should. Or perhaps the slave cylinder needs to have some washers installed between it and the bracket it is mounted to.<P>If you can't get the car into gear without grinding the gears (even though the pedal is all the way to the floor), or if the pedal feels mushy and it takes a great deal of effort to grt the car into 1st gear from neutral when the engine is running and the car is standing still, then you most likely have air (or a leak) in your clutch mater cylinder-to-slave cylinder piping.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-16-2001||04:37 PM||||Does the pedal have the same amount of travel as it did befor eyou started having trouble?<P>Formula is right.  The hydraulics are used  to disengage the clutch.  If they are weak then you won't be able to totally disengage the clutch.<P>Several things could be happening:<P>The clutch friction material is shot causing the clutch to slip.  This requires a new clutch.<P>The throwout bearing could be binding on the shaft and not letting the clutch fully engage.  This would require pulling the transmission and freeing up the throwout bearing.  And since you are this far into the clutch it would be foolish not to change it at this time.<P>The pressure plate springs are broken or shot.  This again would require changing the clutch.<P>You could have oil leaking from the engine onto the clutch friction material.  If it is from the crankshaft then you'll have to pull the transmission to fix it and you might as well change out the clutch while it is apart.<P>If you are at all handy with mechanical things and have a place to work on the car changing the clutch isn't a terrible job.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gerald||10-16-2001||04:52 PM||||Well for starters if you do need a new clutch it wont cost 1000 dollers. Thats just crazy talk. Dont get a oem clutch kit. They cost too much and dont grip as well as the jobber clutch I got. From what it sounds like you DO need a clutch. If you cant doit yourself just shop around. Im sure you can find a place that will do it for a lot less then a GM dealer. Shouldnt cost no more then 500 US.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Simple Fiero||10-16-2001||06:20 PM||||500US is around 750CND. Which I just can't afford heck I can't even afford the 400 for winters, so I am going to have to say the hell with it and park it in about a week for winter and decide over winter what to do with it. I realize that the clutch is just part of matinence, and I am at a 103kms. So I guess it is just time I guess.||||reg||1
