Z||000008||Turbo88||10-16-2001||11:18 PM||||If you have access to hand tools and a couple floor jacks, you can do it yourself for around 250 bucks US. It's not as bad as you might think. I would perfer pulling the cradle on my 88 Formula anyday vs my 99 T/A. Once the cradle is out, everything is right there to work on! I pulled the cradle, tore apart two transmissions, replaced exhaust manifolds, plugs, and misc stuff in a weekend with a garage. <P>But no matter how you go about it, it shouldn't cost you 1k CDN to do a clutch swap, even with the clutch... ||||reg||1
